cimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  tan gray to white  fibrous mass  coming to within 0 2cm from the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1  now as A  Additional representative sections of the lesion are submitted in cassettes B through E  Representative sections of tissue away from the lesion are submitted in cassettes F through H  Resident  LAN WANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ADRIANO PIRIS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Present.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 14 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  FOCAL  INVOLVING 3 OF 20 SLIDES  SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MULTIPLE MICROSCOPIC FOCI  3  SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMAS  SEVERAL  4  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS IN ASSOCIATION WITH MICROCALCIFICATION  5  RADIAL SCARS  SEVERAL  6  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES IN ASSOICATION WITH MICROCALCIFICATION  NOTE  Invasion of stroma  lymphatic or blood vessels is not identified  The margin of resection is free of carcinoma  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  AS MEASURED FROM THE GLASS SLIDE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIFOCAL  HIGH AND LOW GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH AND AWAY FROM THE MASS  WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES AND PRESENT AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  3  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  EXTENSIVE  IN ASSOCIATION WITH MICROCALCIFICATION  NOTE  No blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The margin of the specimen appears free of invasive carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 29 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in two parts and accompanied by radiographs  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma and fatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted in A through J   and U   DD  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white firm area  1 0cm from the closest margin  The firm area are submitted in K through L  Representative sections from the remainder in M through T  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  LEFT BREAST   NO AREAS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DX   RIGHT BREAST   SUSPICIOUS AREA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Absent.
