 REMOVED_CASE_ID  GILBERT CAROL A 48 F  REG REF 06 01    REMOVED_CASE_ID   WIC RICHARD JEANNE M D                                                                                             Specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received  06 01 09  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type    Clinical diagnosis   history  A small group of indeterminate calcifications of right breast  upper outer quadrant    fibrocystic changes vs ductal carcinoma in situ Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  stereo breast biopsies  right breast  and consists of two cassettes designated on the specimen requisition to contain calcifications  The first cassette is orange and contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  aggregate of firm  yellowish pink  glistening needle biopsies  each measuring REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm  in diameter  The specimens are marked with black ink  The second cassette is aqua and contains three firm  yellowish pink  glistening needle biopsies measuring 1 5cm  in length x 0 3cm  in diameter to 2cm  in length x 0 3cm  in diameter  The specimens are marked with black ink  Also present  free floating in the container  is a 2 x 2 x 0 3cm  aggregate of firm  yellowish pink  glistening needle biopsies admixed with blood clot  each measuring 0 3cm  in diameter  The specimens are marked with black ink  Section code  1   tissue in orange cassette  1 agg  all  2   tissue in aqua cassette  3X all  2   free floating tissue  1 agg  all  Total fixation time is REMOVED_DATE hours  Dictated by  LV Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ DIAGNOSIS  Right breast  upper outer quadrant   needle biopsy  Focal atypical intraductal hyperplasia with calcifications  Lobular carcinoma in situ  focal  Columnar cell change with calcifications  Adenosis with calcifications  Focally ruptured ectatic duct with calcification  Focal fibroadenomatous change  Detached fragment of beni