ons with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm pink tan to yellow firm fragment of breast tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm well defined red brown granular mass with scattered yellow nodules  abutting inked resection margins  The remaining parenchyma is white  firm  and soft yellow  A touch prep of the lesion is done  No frozen section is done  Representative sections are submitted in A H  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     TOUCH PREP DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST   POSITIVE FOR MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D  O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Douglas B  Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Absent.
